Bugfix: Parallel WebDAV requests no longer fail at the session lock

With sessions in Redis (phpredis with session locking, 100 retries of 20 ms),
parallel requests of the same session queued up at the session lock. The
desktop client sends its single PROPFIND requests after a bulk upload in
parallel, each with its Bearer token and the session cookie. Under load the
last requests waited longer than 2 seconds, phpredis gave up, the session start
failed silently, the session cookie was deleted and the request ended with
"503 Internal Server Error"; a browser request in the same situation got a 500
and was logged out.

Requests of sync clients (Authorization header plus session cookie on
remote.php, session already authenticated for WebDAV) now release the session
lock right after reading the session and writing LAST_ACTIVITY. This applies to
Bearer tokens and app passwords, and to real passwords via Basic auth unless
the periodic password check is due: then the first of the parallel requests
keeps the lock, checks the password once and the others see the result.
Changes made later in such a request are merged into the freshly read session
on close.
If the lock still cannot be acquired in time, the request continues with a
read-only session (phpredis 6.3 and later) or without a session, the session
cookie is kept, and a warning in the log names the cause. Browser sessions keep
the previous behaviour.
